        &hellip;conservation <span class="search-hit mathjax">hypothesis</span> is found.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('1408.1299v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('1408.1299v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="1408.1299v2-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        A search for $CP$ violation using $T$-odd correlations is performed using the four-body $D^0 \to K^+K^-π^+π^-$ decay, selected from semileptonic $B$ decays. The data sample corresponds to integrated luminosities of $1.0\,\text{fb}^{-1}$ and $2.0\,\text{fb}^{-1}$ recorded at the centre-of-mass energies of 7 TeV and 8 TeV, respectively. The $CP$-violating asymmetry $a_{CP}^{T\text{-odd}}$ is measured to be $(0.18\pm 0.29\text{(stat)}\pm 0.04\text{(syst)})\%$. Searches for $CP$ violation in different regions of phase space of the four-body decay, and as a function of the $D^0$ decay time, are also presented. No significant deviation from the $CP$ conservation <span class="search-hit mathjax">hypothesis</span> is found.
